\title{ZTRecur: Analysis for Zero-Truncated Recurrent Event Data}
\description{
This package provides nonparametric and Cox-type regression methods for analyzing zero-truncated recurrent event data with supplementary information. Key features include estimating rate and mean functions under nonparametric marginal models; estimating time-constant regression coefficients under standard and stratified Andersen-Gill (AG) models; and estimating time-varying covariate effects under stratified and nonstratified Cox-type models. Standard errors (SEs) are estimated using sandwich-based variance estimators for nonstratified models and resampling-based procedures for stratified models. For further details, see Chen, Hu, and Rosychuk (2026) \doi{10.1214/25-AOAS2130}, Chen et al. (2026) \doi{10.1002/cjs.70064}, and Chen, Hu, and Rosychuk (2026) \url{https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.26210}.
}
